   "sentence": "## The five requirement fields, and their sources | field | requirement | source (external, at cite) | |:--|:--|:--| | `cancel` | cancellativity is the door predicate | `arXiv:1502.05580` Lemma 2.3 (*\"simplifiable\"*) | | `neg` / `add_neg` | signed classes | the symmetrization requirement | | `finPart` / `archPart` | ℤ at finite places, ℝ at ∞, **fused in one object** | `arXiv:2205.01391` (Arakelov divisors) | | `act` | the action is by **endomorphisms, not translations** | `arXiv:2602.15941` (*\"a decisive departure\"*) | | `pair` | a biadditive pairing into an ordered target | the absence itself | ## The three open slots, and why they are NOT fields `Definite`, `Nondegenerate`, `SeesTheZeros` are defined as *predicates on candidates*, never as requirements of the structure.",
